# AI-Generated Replies

> Backend is NOT ready yet. Frontend foundation is in place with a mock provider.

## Architecture

```
features/ai-reply/
├── ai-reply.types.ts    ← AiAction, AiReplyRequest/Response, AiReplyProvider, streaming
├── ai-reply.model.ts    ← Zustand store: status, suggestions, streaming, generate/abort
├── ai-reply.api.ts      ← Mock provider + HTTP provider stub (SSE streaming)
├── ai-reply.ui.tsx       ← SmartReplySuggestions, AiActionMenu, AiComposerButton
└── index.ts              ← Public barrel
```

## Use Cases

| Action | Input | Output | UX |
|--------|-------|--------|-----|
| `smart-reply` | Last N messages | 3 short reply chips | Google Messages-style chips above composer |
| `generate-reply` | Thread context | 1 full reply draft | Streamed into preview panel |
| `rewrite` | User's draft | 1 improved version | Replace draft in composer |
| `fix-grammar` | User's draft | 1 corrected version | Replace draft |
| `change-tone` | Draft + tone | 1 rephrased version | Professional/Casual/Friendly/Formal/Concise |
| `translate` | Draft + target lang | 1 translated version | Replace draft |
| `summarize` | Thread messages | 1 summary | Show in preview panel |

## Store (useAiReplyStore)

```ts
import { useAiReplyStore, setAiReplyProvider, createMockProvider } from "~/features/ai-reply";

// Setup (once, in app initialization)
setAiReplyProvider(createMockProvider()); // or createHttpProvider(baseUrl)

// Generate smart replies
await useAiReplyStore.getState().generate({
  action: "smart-reply",
  messages: recentMessages,
  chatContext: { type: "stream", streamName: "general", topic: "hello" },
});

// Read state
const { status, suggestions, streamingText, error } = useAiReplyStore.getState();
// status: "idle" | "loading" | "streaming" | "done" | "error"

// Accept a suggestion (returns text, clears state)
const text = useAiReplyStore.getState().acceptSuggestion(suggestion.id);

// Abort generation
useAiReplyStore.getState().abort();

// Dismiss without accepting
useAiReplyStore.getState().dismiss();
```

## UI Components

### Smart Reply Chips

```tsx
import { SmartReplySuggestions } from "~/features/ai-reply";

// Above the composer:
<SmartReplySuggestions onAccept={(text) => sendMessage({ content: text })} />
```

Shows 3 contextual quick-reply chips. Visible only when `lastAction === "smart-reply"` and `status === "done"`.

### AI Action Menu

```tsx
import { AiActionMenu, AiComposerButton } from "~/features/ai-reply";

const [aiMenuOpen, setAiMenuOpen] = useState(false);

// In composer toolbar:
<AiComposerButton onClick={() => setAiMenuOpen(!aiMenuOpen)} active={aiMenuOpen} />

// Above composer (positioned absolutely):
<AiActionMenu
  draft={composerValue}
  onInsert={(text) => setComposerValue(text)}
  open={aiMenuOpen}
  onOpenChange={setAiMenuOpen}
/>
```

Shows: Generate reply, Rewrite, Fix grammar, Change tone (5 options), Translate, Summarize thread.
Actions that need a draft are disabled when composer is empty.

### Streaming Preview

When `generateStream` is used, the UI shows text appearing token-by-token with a blinking cursor. User can Stop or wait for completion, then Insert or Discard.

## Providers

### Mock (for development)

```ts
import { createMockProvider } from "~/features/ai-reply";
setAiReplyProvider(createMockProvider());
```

Returns canned responses after 300-800ms delay. Smart replies are context-aware (questions, greetings, default). Streaming simulates word-by-word output.

### HTTP (when backend is ready)

```ts
import { createHttpProvider } from "~/features/ai-reply";
setAiReplyProvider(createHttpProvider("https://api.workspace.com"));
```

Endpoints:
- `POST /ai/reply` — non-streaming (returns AiReplyResponse)
- `POST /ai/reply/stream` — SSE streaming (Server-Sent Events, `data: { delta, done, index }`)

## Message Context

The `AiMessageContext` array provides thread context to the LLM:

```ts
interface AiMessageContext {
  id: number;
  senderId: number;
  senderName: string;
  content: string;      // plain text (stripped HTML)
  timestamp: number;
  isOwn: boolean;       // whether current user sent this
}
```

Prepare from `MockMessage[]`:
```ts
const context: AiMessageContext[] = messages.slice(-20).map(m => ({
  id: m.id,
  senderId: m.sender_id,
  senderName: m.sender_full_name,
  content: stripHtml(m.content),
  timestamp: m.timestamp,
  isOwn: m.sender_id === currentUserId,
}));
```

## Rules for AI Agent

### When integrating into composer

1. **Smart replies** — trigger after receiving a new message (not own), with last 10-20 messages as context
2. **Action menu** — show via ✨ button in composer toolbar
3. **Insert = replace** — when user accepts rewrite/translate/fix, replace the composer draft entirely
4. **Insert = append** — when user accepts generate-reply, append to composer (don't replace)
5. **Track with analytics** — `AnalyticsEvent.AI_REPLY_GENERATED`, `AI_REPLY_ACCEPTED`

### Security / Privacy

- **Do NOT send message content to third-party APIs** without explicit user consent
- **Strip HTML** before sending to LLM — use `stripHtml()` from `~/shared/lib/html`
- **Limit context** — max 20 messages, no file attachments
- **Do NOT store** generated suggestions in localStorage or send to analytics
- **Model transparency** — show which model generated the response (`response.model`)

### When backend is ready

1. Replace `createMockProvider()` with `createHttpProvider(baseUrl)` in app initialization
2. Add `VITE_AI_API_URL` env var
3. Add auth header (use existing API client middleware)
4. Handle rate limiting (429) with backoff
5. Add feature flag to enable/disable AI features per organization
